{
  "manufacturer": "inepro Metering",
  "manufacturer_slug": "inepro-metering",
  "model": "PRO380-Mod three-phase energy meter",
  "model_slug": "pro380-mod",
  "short_model": "PRO380-Mod",
  "aliases": [
    "PRO380 Mod",
    "PRO380-Mod CT",
    "PRO380-MOD",
    "inepro PRO380",
    "PRO380 MID"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Energy meter",
  "applies_to": "PRO380-Mod and PRO380-Mod CT (RS485 Modbus RTU), current register map from PRO380 user manual version 2.18-8.",
  "summary": "The PRO380-Mod is inepro's MID-certified three-phase DIN-rail energy meter (direct connection up to 100 A, or a CT version) with an RS485 Modbus RTU port. Every measurement is an IEEE 754 float sent high word first and read with function 03 from hex address blocks 4000h (setup), 5000h (live values) and 6000h (energy). This map covers phase voltages, currents, powers, power factor, frequency, total/tariff/per-phase energy and the writable address, baud, parity, tariff, S0 and combination-code settings.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 1,
    "baud": 9600,
    "parity": "Even",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "hex 0-based",
    "note": "The map prints addresses in hex and they go into the request unchanged: the manual's example frames are 01 06 4003 000A (set Modbus ID) and 01 06 6048 0002 (set tariff). So 4003h is wire address 16387 and 5012h (total active power) is 20498. Do not enter the hex numbers as decimal."
  },
  "default_word_order": "ABCD",
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "PRO380 Series MID Three phase energy meter PRO380-S, PRO380-Mb, PRO380-Mod - User manual",
    "doc_number": "Version 2.18-8",
    "revision_date": "2026",
    "url": "https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6617f74190bf0a53bfd776e8/69f0b42e8df8da5157fb250d_PRO380%20user%20manual%20V2.18-8.pdf",
    "pages": "RS485 spec p. 9; display menus and settings pp. 15-19; Modbus communication p. 26; register map and write commands pp. 27-28 (Appendix A3.2)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "The PDF is the user manual linked from the official PRO380-Mod product page (ineprometering.com/product/pro380-mod-electricity-meter, documentation tab).",
    "'Float ABCD' in the map = IEEE 754 32-bit float, high word first. 'Signed' rows are 16-bit integers.",
    "Units are as printed: power in kW, kvar and kVA (not W), energy in kWh and kvarh.",
    "Left out: Voltage (5000h), Current (500Ah) and Error code (4015h) - the map marks them 'PRO1 only'.",
    "Left out: serial number (4000h), meter code (4002h), CT ratio (400Ch), LCD cycle time (4010h), checksum (401Bh) and active status word (401Dh). They are typed only as 'HEX' with no encoding given; the LCD-time example writes 0025 for 25 s, which suggests BCD. Current direction (4012h-4014h, 'ASCII') and CT mode (401Fh) are left out because their values are not described.",
    "S0 output rate (400Dh) accepts 10000, 2000, 1000, 100, 10, 1, 0.1 or 0.01 imp/kWh.",
    "The manual says the older V1.14 register map still works; it is not covered here.",
    "Baud rates differ between sections: the RS485 spec lists 1200-9600, the Modbus appendix and display menu also list 300 and 600 (and 2400). 9600, 4800 and 1200 appear in every list.",
    "The day-counter write row prints a register length of 1, but its example frame writes 2 registers (4 zero bytes) with function 16; it is listed here as a 2-register float."
  ],
